# Preserve Comments

Comments in this repo are intentional documentation (design intent, timing
contracts, bring-up notes, historical pitfalls). Treat them as first-class
source, not noise.

## Do not
- Delete, strip, or "clean up" existing comments while editing nearby code
- Rewrite a file in a way that drops comments that were already present
- Remove comments because they feel redundant, outdated-looking, or verbose
- Drop inline markers on constants, table rows, or magic values

## Do
- Keep comments when refactoring, renaming, moving, or reformatting code
- Update a comment in place when the code it describes changes, so it stays true
- Add new comments when introducing non-obvious behavior
- Only remove or rewrite comments when the user **explicitly** asks to

## When moving code
- Move the associated comments with the code
- If a comment no longer applies after a real behavior change, revise it — do
  not delete it silently
